+<a id="draft-b01-deferred-context-composite-admission-2026-09-16-authority-review-required"></a>
+### Draft B01 deferred-context composite admission (2026-09-16; authority review required)
+
+This draft defines a distinct private diagnostic admission posture. It does not
+amend ordinary native restart admission: an accepted resident presented without
+the complete authenticated deferred composite continues to take the existing
+resident-only guard and refuse. It does not authorize physical evaluation, a
+provider invocation, a public API, a persisted schema, a general restart path,
+or production activation.
+
+The composite contains the immutable accepted soil resident and its exact
+soil-owner projection in the coupled clock, while the original prepared
+continuation remains separate non-owner custody. The committed bootstrap is a
+third, distinct lineage value. Authentication must bind source/build/map
+allowance; run, policy, configuration, ordered OFE/layer topology and logical
+revision; original prepared support, transaction, predecessor, state and
+receipt-chain lineage; every ordered accumulated operand, trial seal,
+high-plus-carry state and predecessor variant; complete accepted clock slab,
+event, snow/phase, pending-parcel and exact-next-support history; and the
+physical-counter proof already required for the inactive native posture.
+Native physical transaction identifiers and logical revisions remain in their
+respective domains and must not be rebased or compared as interchangeable
+counters.
+
+The required clock-to-credit relationship is source-defined correspondence,
+not equality of aggregates. The current serialized deferred credit groups retain
+the original owner, final trial, accumulated operands and ordered layer-credit
+chain, but do not by themselves establish a per-child support, transaction or
+event key. No admission may infer that mapping from eight accepted clock slabs,
+twelve credit groups, ordinal proximity, or aggregate totals. Before any proof
+may be minted, an independently retained record must establish the complete
+mapping and its owner, support, transaction, event and receipt-chain joins. If
+such evidence is absent, incomplete, foreign, duplicated, reordered or altered,
+the diagnostic must fail closed with the owning custody/clock error and preserve
+every owner byte. The observed eight slabs and twelve credit groups establish no
+count equality rule and no supported admission relation.
+
+Provider/GSI phase authority is independent from these joins. The prior
+committed receipt must be authenticated from an authoritative retained preimage
+or the separately authorized deterministic native provider-prefix procedure;
+the captured tuple alone is insufficient. The current prepared receipt is
+separately validated against its forcing and beginning state/cursor. Both may
+coexist without advancing a live owner. An unavailable authoritative prior
+receipt leaves this admission posture `HOLD`; it may not be repaired by copying
+the prepared digest or by choosing a new seed.
+
+Only after all joins succeed may semantic validation mint an opaque,
+process-local proof for this exact composite. Decoding or digest comparison
+alone never mints it. The proof cannot be serialized, copied to an ordinary
+entrypoint, reused after reconstruction, or retained after any attempt to use
+the existing later replay/install boundary. It admits no resident replacement:
+the resident remains unchanged and deferred custody remains non-owner until
+that one existing boundary completes its canonical full replay and atomic
+install. Any failed validation or failed promotion preserves every live and
+captured owner byte and invalidates the proof. A successful canonical boundary
+installs only its canonical owner/receipt/restart bundle and also invalidates
+the proof; it never installs deferred custody directly.
+
+`INV-LANDSURFACEENERGY-167` and `OBL-LANDSURFACEENERGY-C-023` are draft
+binding additions. They require two independent authority reviews and
+contract-derived red evidence before implementation. The applicable existing
+cross-contract constraints remain `INV-SURFACELIQUID-027` for owner/receiver
+custody, `INV-COUPLEDTIME-031` for inactive-prefix chronology, and
+`SC-SNOWFREEFORCING-001` section 7 for daily receipt identity; this amendment
+does not redefine any of them.
+
